1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,770
If Michael Myers is

2
00:00:01,790 --> 00:00:04,330
ever standing outside your house...

3
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:05,970
do not look away.

4
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:07,920
Count the knives.

5
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:09,870
Do not hide in the closet.

6
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:12,250
And never check if he is dead.

7
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:15,540
This is Instruction 444.

8
00:00:15,990 --> 00:00:17,810
There are four rules.

9
00:00:17,830 --> 00:00:19,570
Follow them exactly.

10
00:00:19,590 --> 00:00:20,930
Otherwise, you will have

11
00:00:20,950 --> 00:00:23,110
to activate the emergency protocol.

12
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:24,990
Rule one.

13
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:26,960
Do not look away.

14
00:00:27,410 --> 00:00:29,180
October thirty-first.

15
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:32,180
Your street is full of masks.

16
00:00:32,210 --> 00:00:33,150
Witches.

17
00:00:33,170 --> 00:00:34,260
Ghosts.

18
00:00:34,290 --> 00:00:37,040
Kids dragging pillowcases full of candy.

19
00:00:37,490 --> 00:00:39,800
But one of them is not moving.

20
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:44,230
A man in a dark jumpsuit and a pale white mask,

21
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:47,740
standing perfectly still under the streetlight across the street.

22
00:00:48,190 --> 00:00:50,480
He is not looking at the houses.

23
00:00:50,510 --> 00:00:52,270
He is looking at your window.

24
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:54,730
Then he tilts his head.

25
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:55,970
Slowly.

26
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,610
Like he is studying you.

27
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:00,210
Do not look away.

28
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:02,010
Not to call someone.

29
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:03,850
Not to close the curtains.

30
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:05,860
Not even to blink for too long.

31
00:01:06,310 --> 00:01:07,970
He never runs.

32
00:01:07,990 --> 00:01:09,300
He does not need to.

33
00:01:09,750 --> 00:01:11,570
Every time you look away,

34
00:01:11,590 --> 00:01:13,200
he is a little closer.

35
00:01:13,590 --> 00:01:14,720
The streetlight.

36
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:16,080
The mailbox.

37
00:01:16,230 --> 00:01:17,210
Your lawn.

38
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,240
And if you look back,

39
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:20,950
and the streetlight is empty...

40
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:23,710
he is already inside.

41
00:01:25,660 --> 00:01:26,990
Rule two.

42
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:28,320
Count the knives.

43
00:01:28,770 --> 00:01:31,740
Before you go to bed, go to the kitchen.

44
00:01:31,810 --> 00:01:33,980
Do not turn on the light.

45
00:01:34,210 --> 00:01:35,340
Count the knives in the

46
00:01:36,250 --> 00:01:37,860
He never brings his own.

47
00:01:38,010 --> 00:01:40,420
He always uses one from your kitchen.

48
00:01:40,870 --> 00:01:41,890
Five slots.

49
00:01:41,910 --> 00:01:43,440
Five handles.

50
00:01:43,590 --> 00:01:44,160
Good.

51
00:01:44,390 --> 00:01:45,840
He is still outside.

52
00:01:46,290 --> 00:01:48,330
But if one slot is empty...

53
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:50,740
do not look for it.

54
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:52,420
Do not call out.

55
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:54,300
Do not check the other rooms.

56
00:01:54,750 --> 00:01:56,760
He is already inside.

57
00:01:56,990 --> 00:01:59,600
And he has your biggest knife.

58
00:02:00,050 --> 00:02:01,870
If you go looking for it,

59
00:02:01,890 --> 00:02:02,980
you will find it.

60
00:02:03,430 --> 00:02:04,530
In the reflection of

61
00:02:04,550 --> 00:02:06,240
the dark kitchen window.

62
00:02:06,630 --> 00:02:07,820
Right behind you.

63
00:02:09,770 --> 00:02:11,220
Rule three.

64
00:02:11,290 --> 00:02:13,430
Do not hide in the closet.

65
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:16,100
You will want to hide in the closet.

66
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:17,250
Everyone does.

67
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,400
He knows that.

68
00:02:18,850 --> 00:02:20,110
Through the slats,

69
00:02:20,130 --> 00:02:21,940
you can see the hallway.

70
00:02:22,050 --> 00:02:23,820
A shape walks past.

71
00:02:24,210 --> 00:02:25,460
Slowly.

72
00:02:25,570 --> 00:02:27,450
Your kitchen knife in his hand.

73
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:30,310
He opens every door in the house.

74
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:32,190
One by one.

75
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:33,350
The bathroom.

76
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:34,710
The laundry room.

77
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:35,830
The guest room.

78
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:37,940
He never hurries.

79
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:40,760
And he always saves the closet for last.

80
00:02:41,510 --> 00:02:43,840
So do not wait for him to reach it.

81
00:02:44,070 --> 00:02:45,890
When he walks out of a room,

82
00:02:45,910 --> 00:02:47,490
slip into it behind him.

83
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:50,140
He never checks a room twice.

84
00:02:50,590 --> 00:02:52,330
If you stay in the closet,

85
00:02:52,350 --> 00:02:55,630
the last thing you see through the slats will be white.

86
00:02:57,480 --> 00:02:58,690
Rule four.

87
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:01,050
Never check if he is dead.

88
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:03,030
You might get lucky.

89
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:04,360
A coat hanger.

90
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:05,640
A knitting needle.

91
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:07,470
Your own kitchen knife.

92
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:08,510
He falls.

93
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:10,810
He lies on the floor.

94
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:12,490
He does not move.

95
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,260
The mask is still on.

96
00:03:14,710 --> 00:03:16,320
Do not go closer.

97
00:03:16,550 --> 00:03:18,760
Do not check if he is breathing.

98
00:03:18,790 --> 00:03:21,150
Do not take the knife out of his hand.

99
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:23,690
Do not turn your back on him.

100
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:25,980
Walk out of the room backwards,

101
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,290
with your eyes on him.

102
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:29,910
Because the moment you turn around...

103
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:34,450
behind you, very slowly, he sits up.

104
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:36,870
He always gets back up.

105
00:03:38,620 --> 00:03:40,230
Emergency protocol.

106
00:03:40,460 --> 00:03:41,800
How to fight back.

107
00:03:42,250 --> 00:03:44,230
If he is standing in front of you,

108
00:03:44,250 --> 00:03:48,500
and there is nowhere left to go, here is what does not work.

109
00:03:48,950 --> 00:03:49,570
Shoot him.

110
00:03:49,590 --> 00:03:51,520
Six times.

111
00:03:51,590 --> 00:03:54,440
He falls from the balcony onto the lawn.

112
00:03:54,550 --> 00:03:57,110
When you look down, the lawn is empty.

113
00:03:57,960 --> 00:03:59,090
Lock the door.

114
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:01,550
He was inside before you locked it.

115
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,930
Get in the car and drive.

116
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:05,660
In the rearview mirror,

117
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:08,070
there is a white face in the back seat.

118
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:09,490
Scream.

119
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:10,660
Your neighbors step

120
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:12,210
out onto their porches.

121
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:14,450
They think it is a Halloween prank.

122
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:15,530
They clap.

123
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:18,460
There is only one thing that works.

124
00:04:18,910 --> 00:04:20,240
Say his name.

125
00:04:20,690 --> 00:04:21,490
Michael.

126
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:24,020
No one has called him by his

127
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:26,290
name since he was six years old.

128
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:28,830
The knife stops in the air.

129
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:30,650
Now say it again.

130
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:32,970
The way his mother used to.

131
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:34,730
Calm.

132
00:04:35,620 --> 00:04:36,430
Michael.

133
00:04:36,740 --> 00:04:37,800
Go home.

134
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:40,600
He tilts his head.

135
00:04:40,990 --> 00:04:42,530
He lowers the knife.

136
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:45,920
Then he turns, walks out of your house,

137
00:04:45,940 --> 00:04:49,710
across the street, and into the empty house on the corner.

138
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:52,450
The one nobody has lived in for years.

139
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:54,790
Do not follow him.

140
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:57,290
Do not watch which window he goes to.

141
00:04:58,040 --> 00:05:00,610
In the morning, the street is quiet.

142
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:02,740
Smashed pumpkins.

143
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,450
Candy wrappers.

144
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:05,010
Police

145
00:05:05,530 --> 00:05:07,990
Your kitchen knife is back in the block.

146
00:05:08,010 --> 00:05:08,630
Clean.

147
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:14,180
Every Halloween since, he stands in the dark window of the empty house,

148
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:15,600
and looks at yours.

149
00:05:16,050 --> 00:05:17,660
He never comes over.

150
00:05:17,890 --> 00:05:19,710
You told him to go home.

151
00:05:19,730 --> 00:05:21,220
He listens to his mother.

152
00:05:21,670 --> 00:05:24,410
But this year, for the first time,

153
00:05:24,430 --> 00:05:25,860
he raises his hand.

154
00:05:26,310 --> 00:05:27,550
He is waving.

155
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:30,410
Do not wave back.

156
00:05:31,860 --> 00:05:35,030
And that was Instruction 444.

157
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:38,180
If this ever happens to you...

158
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:39,530
you know the protocol.
